                                "level": 1,
                                "elements": "Simplification is the reduction of an expression to its most compact form. This function combines like terms, reduces fractions, eliminates redundant operations. If the original formula became cumbersome after intermediate computations, this makes it concise and readable. The result can be presented in real, fractional, or complex numbers (selected via the context menu on the result).",
